## File Generation Settings

**IMPORTANT**: When generating files, create ALL files immediately without asking for permission on each file, even when creating a file outside the current directory. Use the write tool to create all necessary project files in sequence.

## Implementation Notes

### Essential Setup Only

- **Create `.nvmrc` file** with the LTS Node.js version (e.g., `lts/iron` or `20`)
- **Keep it minimal** - only include packages that are absolutely necessary for the chosen stack
- Generate a basic Prisma schema with ONLY a User model (id, email, createdAt, updatedAt), but do not run migrations
- For full-stack projects, create ONE simple "Hello World" resolver/endpoint that returns a string
- Do NOT create authentication systems, complex schemas, or business logic
- Do NOT anticipate future needs - user can add features later

### Package Management

- **Use LATEST stable versions of ALL dependencies** - ALWAYS check npm.com for current versions using web_search
- Search npm.com for EACH major dependency before adding it to package.json
- When specifying package versions, use caret ranges (e.g., `^6.0.0`) to allow patch/minor updates
- Verify current versions by searching "npm [package-name] latest version" on npm.com
- Check for peer dependency compatibility (e.g., React version requirements for UI libraries)
- Only install packages required for the basic setup
- Never use outdated or deprecated package versions

### Code Standards

- Include proper TypeScript configurations with strict mode (as documented in tech docs)
- Set up environment variable validation with Zod schemas
- **ALWAYS use Material-UI (MUI) + Emotion for styling - NEVER use Tailwind CSS**
- Use MUI components for the simple Hello World page
- Follow idiomatic React conventions from `FRONTEND_TECH_STACK.md` or `NEXTJS-TECH-STACK.md`:
  - Pages in `src/pages/` with `Page` suffix (Vite) or `src/app/*/page.tsx` (Next.js)
  - Features in `src/features/` (Vite) or route-specific folders (Next.js)
  - Shared components in `src/components/`
  - GraphQL operations in `src/graphql/` (Full-Stack Only)
  - Path aliases `~/` configured

